localsend-desktop (the app's display name is LocalSend) is built on, and
redistributes in source form:

- LocalSend, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/localsend/localsend
  The official protocol core (crate `localsend`) is vendored unmodified at
  `vendor/localsend` from upstream commit 92e133aa43869e94d394fd04fa70c50a0f796a64;
  see `vendor/localsend/UPSTREAM.md` and `vendor/localsend/LICENSE` (the full
  Apache License 2.0 text). No changes were made to it. The packaged `.app`
  bundles these license texts under `Contents/Resources/`.

- LocalSend visual identity reference, Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/localsend/localsend/tree/main/app/assets/img
  The icon in `design/AppIcon.icon` and the runtime mark in `src/ui/icons.rs`
  are a new vector reinterpretation of LocalSend's central node and segmented
  orbit motif, rather than copies of the upstream PNGs. `assets/icon.png`
  is rendered from these layers by Apple's Icon Composer for platforms
  without native layered icon support. The reference license is retained as
  `assets/LocalSend_LICENSE.txt`, bundled as LICENSE-LocalSend-logo on macOS
  and among the NSH assets on every platform.

- Material Icons font (Material Icons, Copyright 2019 Google LLC),
  CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  `assets/MaterialIcons-Regular.otf`, taken unmodified from the Flutter SDK's
  `material_fonts` artifact, draws the fingerprint icon view LocalSend's
  verification page uses. Its license text ships as
  `Contents/Resources/LICENSE-MaterialIcons` in the macOS bundle and as
  `MaterialIcons_LICENSE.txt` among the app's NSH assets on every platform.

- Native Shell (nsh), Apache-2.0, https://github.com/longbridge/nsh
  The UI framework this app is written in (engine, renderer, platform hosts).
  Its `examples/gallery-rs` was read for API technique (adaptive colors,
  canvas icons, layout/motion patterns); no gallery source file is copied.

Third-party Rust crates: the dependency tree is predominantly MIT and/or
Apache-2.0 (plus BSD/ISC/Zlib/Unicode/CDLA-Permissive licenses and one MPL-2.0
crate, `option-ext`, pulled in by nsh); there is no GPL/AGPL code. The full,
revision-pinned list is available from `cargo tree --locked --format '{p} {l}'`
and is checked by `cargo deny` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `deny.toml`).

References read for architecture and design only (no source copied):
- Noop, MIT, https://github.com/huacnlee/noop
- Omasend, MIT, https://github.com/huacnlee/omasend

This app's own source is MIT; see LICENSE.
